{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_jd2tui4l3g6t26hemjw3xqbfetmlzahv2du4yvzvfmmaw2bcpada","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass, `verify.sh` exits 0, and the C sources are untouched (original 01:57 timestamps).\n\n## What the project turned out to be\n\n`c_src/` contains a single 68-line translation unit (`main.c`) with 6 functions and **no** `#ifdef`s, CMake options, or Cargo features — so there is exactly **one** valid build configuration (`CONFIGS.md` documents the enumeration: `--no-default-features` ≡ default ≡ `--all-features`).\n\n## Changes made to the Rust side\n\n- **`src/imp.rs`** (new) — the behaviour, moved off `&str` onto raw `&[u8]`, because `printf(\"%s\\n\", line)` copies bytes and never validates UTF-8. Writes go straight to fd 1.\n- **`src/lib.rs`** (new) — `cdylib` with `#[no_mangle] extern \"C\"` exports `printLine`, `bad`, `good`, `main`, matching the C `.so` exactly; `static helperBad`/`helperGood` stay unexported.\n- **`src/main.rs`** — thin wrapper; includes `imp.rs` by path so the lib's exported `main` can't collide with the bin's entry symbol.\n- **`Cargo.toml`** — added `[lib] crate-type = [\"rlib\",\"cdylib\"]`, `[features] default = []`, dev-deps `libloading`/`libc`.\n\n## Artifacts\n\n`SYMBOLS.md` (4/4 C symbols exported, symbol diff = 0, 0 unresolved non-libc), `ERRORS.md` (11 rows, all with passing tests; E11 documented N/A — the C API has no enum), `CONFIGS.md` (20 rows, all checked), `VERIFICATION.md`, `verify.sh`.\n\n## Tests — 34 total, all passing, both sides loaded via `libloading`\n\n`differential_valid.rs` (20 = C1–C20, ~1800 randomized cases, fixed seed), `differential_errors.rs` (10 = E1–E10), `symbol_parity.rs` (4).\n\n## Two harness bugs I found and fixed — worth flagging\n\n1. **`cargo test` never rebuilds the `cdylib`.** It compiles the lib only as an `rlib`, so tests were loading a stale `target/debug/libdriver.so`. I caught this via mutation testing: a deliberately broken `bad()` was *not* detected. The harness now does a nested `cargo build --lib` into a private target dir (avoiding the outer build lock) and forwards feature flags via `CDIFF_CARGO_ARGS`.\n2. **libtest's progress output polluted the captures.** Its \"test … ok\" lines are written to the process-global `io::stdout()` from another thread and landed in the redirected fd 1. `capture()` now holds the `StdoutLock` across the redirect window, so it is parallelism-proof without `--test-threads=1`.\n\n## Non-vacuity evidence (mutations applied to Rust, then reverted)\n\n| mutation | result |\n|---|---|\n| `bad()` also calls `helper_bad()` | detected by E3/E9/E10/C11/C16/C17/C18 |\n| `print_line` via `String::from_utf8_lossy` | detected by E3/E5/E6/C5/C7/C16/C19 |\n| `#[no_mangle]` removed from `good` | detected by symbol parity (`missing: [\"good\"]`) |\n\nOne judgement call worth stating explicitly: the exported `printLine` writes **unbuffered** to fd 1, whereas C's `puts` goes through the fully-buffered `stdout`. The byte streams are identical (every write is a whole line, and the harness `fflush(NULL)`s the C side before comparing), but it is a deliberate deviation in buffering, not a byte-level one — verified end-to-end for both pipe and file redirection in C18."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":628,"cache_read_input_tokens":115138,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":628,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34287324-215e-4705-80a5-e36a13a24924","uuid":"d9fc37ca-f1e2-4f15-80e7-79c2ea964d21","timestamp":"2026-08-18T02:14:02.479Z"}
